Short answer: it’s safest to use the exact name that’s on your Social Security card (your legal name as SSA has it). Many organizations match the name you give to the SSN on file, and mismatches can cause delays, rejected forms, or verification problems.

Notes and practical guidance:
- Match the SSA record: For anything that will be checked against the Social Security Administration (employment, tax forms, benefits, some bank verifications), use the same first name, middle name/initial, last name and suffix exactly as they appear on your Social Security card.
