- Middle names/initials: If your Social Security card includes a middle name or initial, include it. If not, omit it.
- Name changes: If you’ve legally changed your name (marriage, court order) but not updated SSA, update SSA first; otherwise use the name currently on the SSA record.
- If the form asks for “legal name” vs “preferred name,” use your legal/SSA name for official/legal fields.
- If you expect a mismatch (e.g., you commonly use a different last name) note it on the form if there is an “also known as” or “other names used” field, or contact the organization to ask their policy.
- Consequences of mismatch: Possible delays in payroll/tax processing, rejected benefits applications, or identity verification failures. For IRS/TIN matching, the name/SSN must match SSA records or the return may be flagged.

